🧠 Intuition
To check if s is a subsequence of t, we don’t need to try all combinations (which would be expensive).

Instead, we can greedily match characters in order:

Traverse string t
Try to match characters of s one by one
If all characters of s are found in order inside t, then s is a subsequence
The key idea is:

A subsequence only requires relative order, not continuity.

⚙️ Approach
Use a pointer j for string s

Iterate through each character c in t

If c == s[j], move j forward

At the end:

If j == s.size(), all characters were matched → return true
Otherwise → return false
💻 Code
class Solution {
public:
    bool isSubsequence(string s, string t) {
        int j = 0;

        for (char c : t) {
            if (j < s.size() && c == s[j]) {
                j++;
            }
        }

        return j == s.size();
    }
};
⏱️ Time Complexity
O(n), where n = t.length()
We scan t exactly once
🧮 Space Complexity
O(1) (constant space)
No extra data structures used
✅ Summary
Efficient single-pass solution
Greedy + two-pointer technique
Optimal for a single query scenario
